ant accepts their aid grudgingly at best)</div> </div> </div> </div>JUJU MAKES YOU FEEL JUST ABSOLUTELY<br /> <img src=\"http://media.tumblr.com/ebf1170ee82826b64ec152ec17d47875/tumblr_inline_mgi8lwFuJa1ruqz7p.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> I Mean Peachy!!!!!!!!!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3239-jane_dargason","name":"Jane_Dargason","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3239_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T14:44:32-07:00","id":183235,"title":"","content":"<b>Oaken Bones</b><br /> <br /> This goblin 'fruit' is very similar to an ordinary potato plant in form, except that it only takes root within a large enough piece of petrified wood. The vaguely bone-shaped edible tubers it produces must be 'mined' by breaking apart the wood they grew inside with a cold iron tool, and then boiled in an iron pot. Any other method of harvesting leaves them powerless and mildly toxic with symptoms similar to uncooked potatoes.<br /> <br /> Eating a properly-prepared Oaken Bone allows individuals to soak lethal damage with their stamina, and they can inflict lethal damage with unarmed attacks. However the changeling is also much heavier, and suffers -1 speed as a result. They will not be able to swim without sinking, and seem to leave deep footprints and dents in things they handle no matter how careful they may be.<br /> <br /> The benefits and penalties persist until the changeling gets a good night's sleep. Oaken Bones are fed with feelings of endurance and overcoming pain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T21:14:33-07:00","id":183493,"title":"","content":"Is soak something they introduced into the system in the GMC? It doesn't exist in vanilla Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T02:44:32-07:00","id":183667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quanutmshard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/16959-fanmade-goblin-fruit-index?p=183235#post183235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Oaken Bones</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Eating a properly-prepared Oaken Bone allows individuals to soak lethal damage with their stamina, and they can inflict lethal damage with unarmed attacks. However the changeling is also much heavier, and suffers -1 speed as a result. They will not be able to swim without sinking, and seem to leave deep footprints and dents in things they handle no matter how careful they may be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Soak is not anymore a thing in nWod. <br /> What about a 1/1 armor (which stacks with other armor) for the duration of the effect?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T22:21:04-07:00","id":184541,"title":"","content":"Duplicating the effects of the Tovil's Ooze oddment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}